{
    "background_story": "Henry was an unlikely candidate for the monastery, having spent his early years as a rugged adventurer. However, after a life-altering experience while traveling abroad, he felt an inexplicable calling to serve a higher purpose. Henry abandoned his worldly pursuits and joined a secluded monastery, where he took vows of poverty, chastity, and obedience. As Brother Henry, he dedicated himself to a life of prayer, contemplation, and service. His rugged past proved to be an asset in unexpected ways, as he used his physical strength to help with manual labor and his worldly experience to counsel troubled souls. Despite initial reservations from his fellow monks, Henry's genuine devotion and compassion earned him a place among the brotherhood. He became known for his wisdom, kindness, and unwavering commitment to his faith.",
